preConditionHook:
// THE FIRST WEAK PULLBACK BAR OF A SPIKE, FADED. After spikeBars consecutive
// bull trend bars ending ONE BAR AGO, the current bar trades below the previous
// bar's low: buy, betting the pullback fails and the spike resumes. Short is
// the mirror.
//
// THE LIMIT FILL IS APPROXIMATED BY THE BAR TRADING THROUGH THE LEVEL, as the
// mining brief allows -- low[0] <= low[1] rather than a resting order. Three
// sources state the same setup (5 bars with a limit at the prior bar's extreme;
// 2 bars with a limit at or below the doji's low; 2 bars as a with-trend stop
// entry on the first bar poking past the prior extreme) and all three fire on
// the same bar. Default spikeBars 2, from two of the three.
//
// KEPT WHOLE: the run must END one bar before the pullback bar, an offset no
// pane can supply, and the pullback half is LaggedHigherHigh negated and
// flipped, which a placement toggle would apply to the run half as well.
//
// NOT FirstPullbackAfterSpike, which retains the pullback bar's HIGHEST price and waits
// for a LATER bar to close above it within a wait window; this rule enters on
// the pullback bar itself, so the two fire on different bars.
//
// NOT BuyOppositeColorBarAfterTrendBarRun, which needs the pullback bar to
// FINISH down and says nothing about where it traded.
//
// The run's bar shape is StrongTrendBarRun's settled definition read at lag 1:
// a strict body direction and a body of at least bodyFraction of the bar's own
// range. The all-of-N loop starts true and lets any failing bar clear the flag,
// so the loop runs unconditionally and EasyLanguage's lack of short-circuiting
// cannot matter. The flags are class members and persist across bars, so both
// are reset at the top.
//
// Products, not quotients: EasyLanguage raises a runtime divide-by-zero and a
// zero-range bar is legal data.
//
// Deepest bar touched: spikeBars.
spikeUp = true;
spikeDn = true;
for (int k = 1; k <= (int)spikeBars; ++k) {
    if (el_le(close[k], open[k])) spikeUp = false;
    if (el_lt(close[k] - open[k], bodyFraction * (high[k] - low[k]))) spikeUp = false;
    if (el_ge(close[k], open[k])) spikeDn = false;
    if (el_lt(open[k] - close[k], bodyFraction * (high[k] - low[k]))) spikeDn = false;
}
